From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-24)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: apply the built-in-provider object flags

Run 40152828517 staged all three payloads for MILANF and then failed
inside them, because the per-object flags that let Apple's kext sources
build inside the kernel are still gated on MACHINE_CONFIG == SWEET.

bsd/conf/Makefile.template: the '-include sweet_hfs_compat.h' plus the
bsd/sweet_hfs include paths never reached the HFS objects, so the compat
header that clears CONFIG_PROTECT was absent. The build then died on
<AppleKeyStore/AppleKeyStoreFSServices.h> (which this tree does not have)
and on the cp_*/ubc_* declarations that header exists to disable. The
sweet_libpthread include paths sit in the same block.

libkern/conf/Makefile.template: the bearssl includes and, more
importantly, -mgeneral-regs-only for the AES/MD5/SHA objects. Those
objects are 'optional crypto' and therefore already compile for MILANF,
but they compiled with FP/SIMD codegen permitted, which kernel code must
never have.

Both gates become a filter over SWEET and MILANF. SWEET's build is
unchanged: the filter matches it exactly as the old equality did.

diff --git a/bsd/conf/Makefile.template b/bsd/conf/Makefile.template
index f2d8bf8..f87b363 100644
--- a/bsd/conf/Makefile.template
+++ b/bsd/conf/Makefile.template
@@ -44,8 +44,10 @@ CFLAGS+= -include meta_features.h -DDRIVER_PRIVATE \
         -Warray-bounds-pointer-arithmetic
 SFLAGS+= -include meta_features.h
 
-# This provider is built into SWEET; other boards use their normal kext.
-ifeq ($(CURRENT_MACHINE_CONFIG),SWEET)
+# These providers are built into the Qualcomm port; other boards use their
+# normal kexts. MILANF stages the same sources (0019/0020/0026), so it needs
+# the same per-object flags.
+ifneq (,$(filter $(CURRENT_MACHINE_CONFIG),SWEET MILANF))
 SWEET_PTHREAD_ROOT = $(SRCROOT)/bsd/pthread/sweet_libpthread
 SWEET_PTHREAD_INC = -I$(SWEET_PTHREAD_ROOT) -I$(SWEET_PTHREAD_ROOT)/private -I$(SWEET_PTHREAD_ROOT)/include
 sweet_pthread_init.o_INCFLAGS = $(SWEET_PTHREAD_INC)
diff --git a/libkern/conf/Makefile.template b/libkern/conf/Makefile.template
index aca295c..7fba503 100644
--- a/libkern/conf/Makefile.template
+++ b/libkern/conf/Makefile.template
@@ -19,7 +19,9 @@ include $(MakeInc_def)
 CFLAGS+= -include meta_features.h -DLIBKERN_KERNEL_PRIVATE -DOSALLOCDEBUG=1
 SFLAGS+= -include meta_features.h
 
-ifeq ($(CURRENT_MACHINE_CONFIG),SWEET)
+# BearSSL sources staged by 0020 compile here for the Qualcomm port; they
+# need their own include tree and must not emit FP/SIMD in kernel code.
+ifneq (,$(filter $(CURRENT_MACHINE_CONFIG),SWEET MILANF))
 SWEET_AES_ROOT = $(SRCROOT)/libkern/crypto/sweet_bearssl
 SWEET_AES_INC = -I$(SWEET_AES_ROOT)/inc -I$(SWEET_AES_ROOT)/src
 sweet_aes.o_INCFLAGS = $(SWEET_AES_INC)
